453	/// Both events must be sequenced as the FIRST record of their own stream
454	/// (`store_seq == 0` each), and a read scoped to generation two must return
455	/// exactly one event. Under the pre-run-axis key the second publish would have
456	/// seen generation one's head, retried, and landed at `store_seq == 1` on
457	/// generation one's stream — one fused transcript, silently.
